WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.001
[music playing]

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:04.070
 Zack, Frank, Nehemiah--
congratulations.

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:06.939
You've made it into the
final round of competition.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:08.708
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:12.779
four five days to recreate an
iconic weapon from history.

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:17.650
The Nzappa zap.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:18.484
 Jazz.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:19.952
 All right,
bladesmiths, good luck.

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:21.454
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.254
 Let's do this.

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:23.489 line:7%
 Uh-huh.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.590 line:7%
[rock music]

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.926 line:0%
ZACK LEWIS: Today we're
here in Sonora, California--

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.794 line:7%
here to make an Nzappa zap.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.563 line:7%
Let's see how this goes.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.966 line:0%
I can't fit it in
here, so I might have

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.467 line:7%
to do this thing old-fashioned.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.336
To be truthfully honest,
I'm scared [bleep]-- less.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:39.405
My master had a
personal emergency.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:42.208
He had to leave the competition,
and now I'm stranded

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.876
here doing this on my own.

00:00:43.942 --> 00:00:45.711
Just got to keep it together.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:46.712
It's amazing.

00:00:46.745 --> 00:00:48.280
I made it this far by myself.

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:49.382
But I'm going to
give it my all--

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:52.851
give 110%-- and
see what I can do.

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:54.854 line:7%
There we go!

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.455 line:7%
 Today it's my turn.

00:00:56.522 --> 00:01:00.026
I got to turn this square piece
of hot metal into a blade.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.828
Nehemiah split it down
the middle of the night

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:05.498
before so that I can pull that
apart, and there's my blade.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:08.334
Zack better be
bringing his game!

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:12.538
The charcoal forge is one of the
most interesting ways to heat

00:01:12.604 --> 00:01:14.874
treat, and what I'm
looking for is an even

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.676
red color all the way across.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:17.843
That's the right
color, Nehemiah.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:18.745
NEHEMIAH BROUSSEAU: Yep.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:23.850
[rock music]

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.018
 Now, let's hear how
this thing sounds.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.753
[scraping on blade]

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:28.754
Awesome.

00:01:28.787 --> 00:01:29.621
NEHEMIAH BROUSSEAU: [whistles]

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:31.123
 It's hard.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.025
Incredible.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.427 line:7%
[rock music]

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:38.263 line:0%
 Day three-- and I'd like to
be a little further than I am.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:41.901
I want this thing to be
perfect before I quench.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.169
[music playing]

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:46.171
I'll go ahead and heat up
my oil little bit here.

00:01:46.238 --> 00:01:47.874
If I want to be "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.542
I got to pull out
all the tricks.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.410
I figure I got to
preheat this stuff.

00:01:51.477 --> 00:01:54.547
You won't have it
around 200 degrees.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:57.149
Never had that going on.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.153
It's really getting a
little bit out of hand--

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:03.188
kind of getting to an
uncontrollable fire.

00:02:03.255 --> 00:02:04.623
I'm a little nervous.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:08.661
I have never felt
anxiety like this before.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:11.230
It's really getting a
little bit out of hand.

00:02:11.296 --> 00:02:13.733
I need that [bleep] Stop sign.

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:17.903
Kind of getting to an
uncontrollable fire.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:18.838
[rock music]

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:20.273
[laughs] Luckily, that worked.

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:22.875
I didn't want to have the
fire department out here.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:26.078
Now I can quench my blade.

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:27.313 line:7%
[rock music]

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:28.347 line:0%
FRANK ALLEN WREN II:
Today is my last day.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.949 line:7%
I'm working this copper cap.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:34.520 line:0%
I've got to get this on here
for part of the decoration.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.221
All right.

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:38.457
Aw, [bleep] damn it!

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:39.492
Crack.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:40.860
I think I'm going to just
go right to the grinder

00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:41.827
and grind it now.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:42.728
NEHEMIAH BROUSSEAU: Yeah?

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:43.962
 [bleep]

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:45.198
[rock music]

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.332
The breaking of the
handle's a little bit

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.767
of a blessing in disguise.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.236
Well, now I got to to hang
onto that right up to the butt.

00:02:50.302 --> 00:02:53.639
The handle was way too thick.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:54.974
Yay!

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.409
I'm glad to be done.

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:57.676
Nehemiah will have it tomorrow.

00:02:57.743 --> 00:03:00.379
He will be sharpening
the blade and getting

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:01.981
it completely finished.

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:05.084
Mr. DeMille, I'm
ready for my close up.

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:06.953 line:0%
ZACK LEWIS: My quench
came out great.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.421
I don't want to be
cocky or anything,

00:03:08.487 --> 00:03:10.389
but the blade's looking awesome.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:13.259
It's got all the intricate
artwork on the steel.

00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:14.627
I really did a weird
hammer pattern,

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:17.263
so it looks like it was made
just rocks in the Congo.

00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:20.933
I'm hoping to put this
Nzappa zap on the mappa map.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.836
First time using it.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.337
[crash]

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:29.608
Think it'll cut--
probably will "keel."

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.609
[dramatic music]

00:03:30.676 --> 00:03:33.546
 Bladesmiths-- now the
Nzappa zap was a brutal

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.415
weapon used in close quarter.

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.316
We'll see how lethal
your weapon is

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.519
when I deliver multiple
strikes on this pig carcass.

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:41.987
Zack, you're up first.
You ready?

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:42.922
 Hell yeah.

00:03:42.988 --> 00:03:45.090
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:48.228
[rock music]

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.268
[music playing]

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:58.671
Well, Zack, that's a hog.

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.005
This is a hog.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:01.140
It is heavy.

00:04:01.206 --> 00:04:02.508
But it's powerful.

00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:05.979
The curve you have in here
digs deep into the chops.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:09.048
Here it lacerated
the spine easily.

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:12.918
Overall, your weapon will kill.

00:04:12.951 --> 00:04:14.286
Frank-- Nehemiah-- your turn.

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:15.554
You ready?
- Play on.

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:16.322
 Play on.

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:18.323
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:21.327
[suspenseful music]

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:25.465
[rock music]

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:33.406
[music playing]

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:36.342
Frank-- Nehemiah--
it's light, so I can

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.212
go hog wild on this carcass.

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:42.548
When you dig in, it
cuts into the spine

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:46.452
and into the ribs and
lacerates quite well.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.922
Your Nzappa zap will kill.

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:52.625
 The pig that Zack's weapon
had might have opened up

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:55.361
a little bit more, but
the truth is the wounds

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:58.364
were just as deep
and just as bad.

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.366
DAVID BAKER: Next up
is the strength test.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.968
Occasionally, the Nzappa
zap was also thrown.

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:05.738
So to test the strength and
durability of your weapons,

00:05:05.804 --> 00:05:09.742
I'm going to throw them into
this wooden target three times.

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:10.943
Zack, you're up.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:11.710
You ready?

00:05:11.777 --> 00:05:12.477
 Be gentle.

00:05:12.544 --> 00:05:14.847
 [laughs] I'm never gentle.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:21.621
[thud]

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:22.221
[music playing]

00:05:22.287 --> 00:05:23.256
ZACK LEWIS: Yeah!

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.258
NEHEMIAH BROUSSEAU: Aw, huzzah!

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.859
[thud]

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.761
 Nice!

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.829
[dramatic musical build]

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:33.800
[thud]

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.335
Yeah!

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:38.704
 Ugh!

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:40.773
[music playing]

00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:43.876
All right, Zack--
it's still tight.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.344
Nothing loosened up.

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:47.046
But right here,
there's a section

00:05:47.112 --> 00:05:50.549
of that blade that's just not
as sharp as the rest of it.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:54.020
There's a roll to that edge,
and that's pretty much right

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.789
where it dug in to the wall.

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.058
Frank-- Nehemiah--
you're up next.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.260
 Play on.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:04.497
[music playing]

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:07.300
 Oof!

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:10.470
[thud]

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:15.108
[thud]

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.209
[dramatic musical build]

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:20.446
[thud]

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:24.851
[music playing]

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:30.056
You can see right here
when the handle hit

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:32.091
the target in its rotation--

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:35.193
but nothing's wrong
with this blade.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.462
it held up.

00:06:36.495 --> 00:06:37.663
Nicely done, guys.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:38.263
 Thank you.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.498
 Thank you.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:40.966
 And anybody who actually
has thrown weapons--

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:44.370
you know that the
handles are disposable.

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:45.271
But the metal?

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:46.439
No.

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:48.708
The metal's designed
to not take the damage.

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:50.509
DAVID BAKER: Next up--
the sharpness test.

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:53.245
We're going to see how well
those blade edges held up.

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:55.080
I'm to cut each
one of these ropes.

00:06:55.147 --> 00:06:56.448
The meat will drop.

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:58.450
I'm going to cut in each
one of those pieces of meat.

00:06:58.517 --> 00:06:59.385
Zack, you're up first.

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:00.152
Are you ready?

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:00.920
 Yes, sir.

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:01.920
DAVID BAKER: OK.

00:07:01.987 --> 00:07:03.121
 I do you feel like me
and Frank and Nehemiah

00:07:03.188 --> 00:07:04.490
are all neck and neck.

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:06.826
It's definitely a
tight race right now.

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:09.328
I've never known what weak
in the knees means before,

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:13.365
but actually my
knees almost hurt.

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:16.569 line:7%
[rock music]

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:29.548
[music playing]

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:31.650
DAVID BAKER: All right,
Zack, though your blade

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:35.555
is sharp in most places,
that roll you picked up--

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.989
I think that's what stopped
it from going through the rope

00:07:38.056 --> 00:07:39.058
immediately.

00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:40.259
But the second cut--

00:07:40.292 --> 00:07:42.261
I caught it down
in here somewhere--

00:07:42.327 --> 00:07:44.096
and it just went right through.

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.398
All in all, that's a cutter.

00:07:46.465 --> 00:07:47.266
 Thank you.

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:49.267
 Frank-- Nehemiah--

00:07:49.301 --> 00:07:50.035
 Play on!

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:51.971
 Play on!

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:54.941
[music playing]

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:59.879
[rock music]

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:08.687
[music playing]

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:12.458
 For cutting rope-- right
off, this divot in the middle

00:08:12.524 --> 00:08:14.793
here actually worked very well.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:17.262
The handle where it
broke on the throw--

00:08:17.329 --> 00:08:18.430
didn't bother me at all.

00:08:18.463 --> 00:08:21.066
It's below were my hand sits.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:22.434
It's a cutter.

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:24.570
Nicely done.

00:08:24.604 --> 00:08:25.704
[dramatic music]

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:27.239
WIL WILLIS: Bladesmiths--
what started out

00:08:27.305 --> 00:08:30.443
as a competition focused on
masters and apprentices working

00:08:30.476 --> 00:08:32.845
together turned into
an apprentice going

00:08:32.912 --> 00:08:35.581
against a master
and his student.

00:08:35.614 --> 00:08:38.450
You rolled with it,
and here we are.

00:08:38.483 --> 00:08:40.419
The judges have made
their final decision,

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:44.389
and the Master and Apprentice
"Forged in Fire" Champion title

00:08:44.456 --> 00:08:47.092
goes to--

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:50.162
[dramatic musical build]

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:52.231
Frank and Nehemiah.

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:54.533
Congratulations, you are
the "Forged in Fire" Master

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.834
and Apprentice Champions.

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:56.468
Good job.

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:57.669
 Thank you.

00:08:57.736 --> 00:08:59.104
WIL WILLIS: Zack,
unfortunately, your blade

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:00.572
did not make the cut.

00:09:00.639 --> 00:09:02.541
 Zack, first let me
commend you for just

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:04.243
pushing through this solo.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.477
 Thank you, sir.

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:06.779 line:0%
DAVID BAKER: You gave
us a lot of artistry

00:09:06.846 --> 00:09:08.247 line:0%
in the forging of your
blade, and that's very

00:09:08.313 --> 00:09:09.615 line:7%
impressive for an apprentice.

00:09:09.682 --> 00:09:11.884 line:0%
But that roll you picked
up in the strength test,

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:14.753 line:0%
combined with that extreme
weight of that piece,

00:09:14.786 --> 00:09:16.588 line:7%
made it very hard to wield.

00:09:16.655 --> 00:09:18.491
And that's why we're
letting you go.

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:19.724
ZACK LEWIS: Understandable.

00:09:19.758 --> 00:09:21.359
 Zack, you get the
heart of a lion, brother.

00:09:21.426 --> 00:09:22.795
 Thank you.

00:09:22.861 --> 00:09:23.996
WIL WILLIS: But at this time,
I have to ask you to please

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:25.597
surrender your weapon.

00:09:25.664 --> 00:09:26.899
ZACK LEWIS: Right now
I'm pretty bummed,

00:09:26.966 --> 00:09:29.668
but Jesse ought to be
proud that I persevered

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:31.103
and stuck through this.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:34.373
Hell, I made it this far, and
I feel like I did pretty good.

00:09:34.439 --> 00:09:37.276
I'm a winner in my own heart.

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:38.344
[music playing]

00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:39.912
Frank-- Nehemiah--
congratulations.

00:09:39.945 --> 00:09:42.815
You are the Master and
Apprentice "Forged in Fire"

00:09:42.882 --> 00:09:43.549
Champions.

00:09:43.616 --> 00:09:44.783
Good job.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.387
That title also comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:48.453 --> 00:09:50.222
All right, gentlemen,
please present

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:51.857
your weapon to the judges.

00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:53.059
 [inaudible]

00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:54.292
NEHEMIAH BROUSSEAU: We won!
FRANK ALLEN WREN II: [laughs]

00:09:54.359 --> 00:09:55.594
NEHEMIAH BROUSSEAU: Yay!

00:09:55.661 --> 00:09:57.029
We were the first Master
and Apprentice Champions.

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:58.797
FRANK ALLEN WREN II: I am
extremely proud of Nehemiah.

00:09:58.864 --> 00:10:00.365
Him and I sharing this--

00:10:00.432 --> 00:10:02.401
that's what I
really do this for.

00:10:02.468 --> 00:10:04.069
I think that the
Nzappa zap that we--

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:07.973
Nzap-- I think that the Nzappa
zap represents exactly us.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.410
And that's why I'm very
happy and very proud of it.

00:10:11.444 --> 00:10:14.747
[music playing]

